### Manual API tests (open in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or in Visual Studio / Rider)
@api = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Log in and copy the token from the response
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "Admin123!" }

### Paste the token here
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 2. List products (search + category filter)
GET {{api}}/api/products?search=monitor
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Low-stock products
GET {{api}}/api/products/low-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Place an order (should succeed)
POST {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Beirut Office Supplies", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }, { "productId": 5, "quantity": 3 } ] }

### 5. Place an order with too much quantity (expect 409 "Not enough stock", nothing saved)
POST {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Big Buyer", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }, { "productId": 2, "quantity": 999 } ] }

### 6. Cancel order 1 (stock goes back)
POST {{api}}/api/orders/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Log in as staff and try to delete a product (expect 403 Forbidden)
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "staff", "password": "Staff123!" }
